# `isolation.verify`

Dry-run the recommended isolation decision end to end and report each check.

**Policy** — read (C0, safe). Capability `ship.isolation.read`.

## Arguments

None.

## Returns

`IsolationVerifyResponse` (JSON).

| field | type |
|-------|------|
| `ok` | `bool` |
| `steps` | `map` |
| `resolved` | `map` |

## Invoke

```
ship ops call isolation.verify --json '{}'
```

Kind: read.

## Example response

```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "steps": [
    {
      "name": "decision_resolves",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "resolved to docker (container)"
    },
    {
      "name": "backend_implemented",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "backend for docker is implemented"
    },
    {
      "name": "no_silent_downgrade",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "decision matches the configured tier"
    }
  ],
  "resolved": {
    "resolved": {
      "strategy": "docker",
      "tier": "container",
      "reason": {
        "os_default": {
          "os": "linux"
        }
      },
      "downgraded": false
    },
    "capabilities": {
      "os": "linux",
      "in_sandbox": false,
      "docker": true,
      "podman": false,
      "youki": null,
      "youki_rootfs": null,
      "lima": null,
      "tart": null,
      "wsl2": false,
      "srt": false,
      "sandbox_exec": false,
      "vz_framework": false,
      "firecracker": false,
      "apple_container": false,
      "fly_cli": false,
      "fly_authed": false
    },
    "user_profile_used": {
      "tier": "container"
    }
  }
}
```
